'''Castrol India Limited''' is an automotive and industrial lubricant manufacturing company. Castrol India is the 2nd largest manufacturer of automotive and industrial lubricants in the Indian lubricant market and owns around 20%<ref>{{Cite web | url=https://www.capitaline.com/SiteFrame.aspx?id=1 | title=Capitaline Databases - Indian Corporate, Indian Company Database, Indian Equity Market, Indian Mutual Fund, Transfer Pricer | access-date=6 September 2015 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20151118102258/https://www.capitaline.com/SiteFrame.aspx?id=1 | archive-date=18 November 2015 | url-status=dead }}</ref>{{failed verification|date=July 2020}} market share in the overall Indian lubricant market.<ref name=":0">{{cite web |url=http://www.hdfcsec.com/Market/Information.aspx?CoCode=292&RptType=History |title=HDFC Securities |publisher=Hdfcsec.com |access-date=22 December 2010 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110126224804/http://hdfcsec.com/Market/Information.aspx?CoCode=292&RptType=History |archive-date=26 January 2011 |df=dmy-all }}</ref> It is part of [[Castrol]] Limited UK (part of [[BP]] Group). It has 5 manufacturing plants that are networked with 400+ distributors,{{Citation needed|date=March 2025}} serving over 70,000 retail outlets.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.castrol.com/castrol/sectiongenericarticle.do?categoryId=8278011&contentId=6005704 |title=Castrol India - Castrol India |publisher=Castrol.com |access-date=22 December 2010 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110213145952/http://www.castrol.com/castrol/sectiongenericarticle.do?categoryId=8278011&contentId=6005704 |archive-date=13 February 2011 |url-status=dead }}</ref>{{Update inline|date=March 2025}}

==History==
In 1910, Castrol India started importing certain automotive lubricants from C C Wakefield & Company, making an entry in the Indian market. In 1979, CIL was incorporated under the name of Indrol Lubricants and Specialities Pvt Ltd.<ref name=":0" /> It was listed on [[Bombay Stock Exchange|BSE]] in 1982, and CIL was converted into a public limited company. CIL had formed a subsidiary Company in the year 1987 under the name of Indtech Speciality Chemicals, Ltd.

On 1 November 1990, the name of the company was changed from Indrol Lubricants & Specialities Ltd. to Castrol India Ltd. It helped to manufacture telephone cable jellies, pharmaceutical jellies, and industrial waxes in technical collaboration with Dussek Campbell, U.K.

As of December 2019, there were talks ongoing between [[Reliance Industries]] and [[BP]] for setting up fuel stations in India where Castrol's products will be sold.<ref>{{cite news |title=Reliance-BP petrol pumps to dent PSU market share: Morgan Stanley |url=https://www.financialexpress.com/industry/reliance-bp-petrol-pumps-to-dent-psu-market-share-morgan-stanley/1801090/ |access-date=15 July 2020 |work=[[The Financial Express (India)]] |date=22 December 2019 |archive-url=https://archive.today/20191223152930/https://www.financialexpress.com/industry/reliance-bp-petrol-pumps-to-dent-psu-market-share-morgan-stanley/1801090/ |archive-date=2019-12-23 |url-status=unfit}}</ref>{{cbignore|bot=InternetArchiveBot}}

